Show execution metrics for a run

Usage: sprocket dev server metrics [OPTIONS] <RUN>

Arguments:
  <RUN>
          The run to report metrics for.

          May be a UUID or the human-readable generated name of the run (e.g. `happy-dolphin-42`).

Options:
      --call <CALL>
          Only report metrics for calls whose call id contains this string

      --json
          Output the raw JSON response instead of the formatted summary

      --host <HOST>
          The hostname of the running Sprocket server to talk to.

          If not provided, falls back to the value in the Sprocket config.

  -p, --port <PORT>
          The port of the running Sprocket server to talk to.

          If not provided, falls back to the value in the Sprocket config.

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease logging verbosity

      --no-ignore
          Ignore `.sprocketignore` files while discovering WDL documents

      --color <COLOR>
          Controls output colorization

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Automatically colorize output depending on output device
          - always: Always colorize output
          - never:  Never colorize output

          [default: auto]

  -m, --report-mode <MODE>
          The report mode for any emitted diagnostics

          Possible values:
          - full:     Prints diagnostics as multiple lines
          - one-line: Prints diagnostics as one line

  -c, --config <CONFIG>
          Path to the configuration file

  -s, --skip-config-search
          Skip searching for and loading configuration files.

          Only a configuration file specified as a command line argument will be used.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
